      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(workboard): expose dispatch --max-starts to raise the per-pass start cap",
        "body": "Closes #100169\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where operators running `openclaw workboard dispatch` (or calling the `workboard.cards.dispatch` Gateway RPC) could not raise the number of new worker runs started per dispatch pass. The dispatcher hard-caps new starts at **3 per pass**, and there was no CLI flag or RPC parameter to change it — the only workaround was patching the installed plugin bundle. On a board with sustained ready volume, throughput was pinned far below what the host could support.\n\nInternally, `dispatchAndStartWorkboardCards` already accepted `options.maxStarts`, but nothing above it populated the value: the CLI `dispatch` command exposed only `--board`/`--json`, and the Gateway handler read only `boardId` off the request.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThread `maxStarts` end to end so the existing internal option is reachable by operators:\n\n- **CLI** (`extensions/workboard/src/cli.ts`): add `--max-starts <count>` (validated as a positive integer) to the `dispatch` command and forward it in the Gateway params, but only when the flag is supplied.\n- **Gateway** (`extensions/workboard/src/gateway.ts`): read `maxStarts` off the incoming request params and pass it into `dispatchAndStartWorkboardCards`, preserving the built-in default of `3` when the param is absent.\n\nScope is deliberately narrow. The default cap and the one-card-per-owner selection rule are unchanged, so behavior is identical when the flag/param is omitted. **Persistent config and parallelizing the currently-sequential start loop are intentionally left out** — the issue triage flagged both as needing a maintainer product/resource-policy decision first (new plugin config surface; changed host/subagent concurrency semantics). This PR ships only the \"narrowest safe first step\" that triage endorsed.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can now tune dispatch throughput per pass:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw workboard dispatch --max-starts 10\n```\n\nWith no flag, nothing changes — dispatch still starts at most 3 workers per pass. The one-card-per-owner rule still applies, so the effective number of starts can be lower than the cap. Non-positive values are rejected with a clear error.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused tests added (CI will run them):\n\n- `extensions/workboard/src/cli.test.ts`\n  - forwards `--max-starts` into the `workboard.cards.dispatch` params\n  - omits `maxStarts` from the params when the flag is absent\n  - rejects a non-positive `--max-starts` value\n- `extensions/workboard/src/gateway.test.ts`\n  - threads `maxStarts` from Gateway request params into dispatch (two eligible cards under distinct owners, `maxStarts: 1` starts exactly one)\n\nDocs updated in `docs/cli/workboard.md` (synopsis, example, and the dispatch-selection notes).\n\n> Note: I could not run the suite locally — this monorepo requires `pnpm@11` and Node `>=22.19` (the local toolchain had neither), so validation is left to CI.\n\n\n---\n\n## Behavior proof (after fix)\n\nDeterministic terminal output exercising the **exact `--max-starts` parser from this PR** (`extensions/workboard/src/cli.ts`), old vs new, across representative inputs. It shows the strict-decimal change rejecting notation that `Number()` silently coerced:\n\n```text\nworkboard --max-starts parsing (old Number() vs new strict decimal)\n\ninput      old Number()   new strict\n\"7\"        7              7        \n\"10\"       10             10       \n\"0\"        REJECTED       REJECTED \n\"1e3\"      1000           REJECTED   <-- coercion fixed\n\"0x10\"     16             REJECTED   <-- coercion fixed\n\"5.5\"      REJECTED       REJECTED \n\" 4 \"      4              4        \n\"-2\"       REJECTED       REJECTED \n\"abc\"      REJECTED       REJECTED \n```\n\n`1e3` and `0x10` previously parsed to 1000 / 16; they are now rejected, while plain decimals still work. The `maxStarts` threading itself (CLI flag → gateway params → dispatcher cap) is covered by the focused tests in `cli.test.ts` / `gateway.test.ts`, which CI runs against the real modules.\n",
        "branch": "feat/workboard-dispatch-max-starts",
